    [BugFix][Quant] Keep the ModelSlim packed module mapping private (#18700)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    `AscendModelSlimConfig._update_packed_modules_mapping()` mutates the
    `packed_modules_mapping`
    it was handed, but that dictionary is the model class's own attribute:
    vLLM's
    `configure_quant_config()` passes `model_class.packed_modules_mapping`
    to the quantization
    config by reference. So the `experts` entry that this method
    auto-discovers from
    `quant_model_description.json` was written straight into the model class
    mapping, which is
    shared by every consumer of that class.
    
    vLLM's LoRA manager reads that very mapping to decide how to pack a
    wrapped module, so once
    the mapping is polluted a quantized MoE layer is routed into the packed
    dummy-LoRA branch,
    whose handling only special-cases `FusedMoEWithLoRA`. Serving a
    ModelSlim W8A8 Qwen3 MoE
    checkpoint together with a 3D MoE LoRA adapter therefore aborted during
    the dummy LoRA
    warmup with:
    
    ```
    AttributeError: 'AscendMoERunner' object has no attribute 'lora_a_stacked'
    ```
    
    BF16 checkpoints were unaffected because no quantization config is built
    for them, so the
    model class mapping stayed clean and the same command worked.
    
    This patch takes a private copy of the mapping before the deltas are
    applied. ModelSlim
    still gets the expert shard names it needs for its own quant-type
    consistency check, and
    nothing leaks into the mapping the rest of the engine reads.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Reproduced on an Atlas A3 node with a ModelSlim W8A8 Qwen3 MoE (35B-A3B)
    checkpoint plus a 3D
    MoE LoRA adapter (`--enable-lora`), which raised the traceback above
    before this change.
    
    CPU-only A/B on the mapping ownership: a model class with
    `packed_modules_mapping = {"gate_up_proj": ["gate_proj", "up_proj"]}` is
    passed to the config
    through `configure_quant_config()`, then
    `_update_packed_modules_mapping()` is called with an
    expert description containing `gate_proj`/`up_proj`/`down_proj` shards.
    
    - Before the change: the model class attribute gains `experts` and
    `config.packed_modules_mapping`
      is still the same object as the class attribute.
    - After the change: the config owns `experts` and the model class
    attribute is untouched.
    
    The exact `AttributeError` path above has not been re-run end-to-end
    yet, since the NPUs on
    that node were fully occupied; I will report the result once the run
    completes.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
